 ## Background
-The Sky Gradient method is a common technique in computer graphics for generating simple sky backgrounds. It is often used in ray marching demos and voxel engines due to its simplicity and visual appeal. Variations include "Aurora Rendering" which adds sine-wave based aurora effects [S2, unofficial], and implementations featuring ground glow and specific color palettes [S4, unofficial]. The technique is widely used in indie games and real-time rendering applications where performance is critical and physical accuracy is not the primary goal.
